---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";

/** Symptoms, in the buyer's language. Recognition is what earns the next scroll. */
const symptoms = [
  {
    title: "Reports arrive too late to act on",
    body: "By the time the monthly pack lands, the month is over. You are steering by looking in the mirror.",
  },
  {
    title: "Three departments, three different numbers",
    body: "Every meeting starts by arguing about whose figure is right instead of deciding what to do.",
  },
  {
    title: "Losses you only find out about afterwards",
    body: "Fraud, defaults and churn get discovered in the reconciliation, not in time to stop them.",
  },
  {
    title: "Expensive people doing typing",
    body: "Analysts and officers spend their days copying data between PDFs, spreadsheets and systems.",
  },
  {
    title: "A dashboard nobody opens",
    body: "Someone built it, it answers the wrong question, and the team went back to Excel.",
  },
  {
    title: "An AI pilot that never shipped",
    body: "It demoed well. Then it hit real data, real volumes and real compliance, and quietly stopped.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section section--alt" id="problem">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--center">
      <p class="eyebrow">The real cost</p>
      <h2>Your data is already telling you where the money is. Nobody is listening.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Every organisation I walk into is sitting on years of transactions,
        tickets, applications and logs. The problem is almost never a lack of
        data. It is that nothing turns it into a decision fast enough to matter.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="problem__grid">
      {
        symptoms.map((item, index) => (
          <li class="card problem__card reveal" data-reveal-delay={index * 60}>
            <span class="problem__mark" aria-hidden="true">
              <Icon name="close" size={14} />
            </span>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <p class="problem__turn">
      If you recognised three or more of these, the gap is not talent or tooling.
      It is that nobody owns the path from raw data to a decision someone acts
      on. <strong>That is the job I do.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 290px), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .problem__card h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .problem__card p {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 0.93rem;
  }

  .problem__mark {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 26px;
    height: 26px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
    color: #c0483c;
    background: rgba(192, 72, 60, 0.12);
  }

  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .problem__mark {
    color: #f08b7f;
    background: rgba(240, 139, 127, 0.14);
  }

  .problem__turn {
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3rem) auto 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.9vw, 1.25rem);
    color: var(--text-2);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
</style>
